From: Device Build maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] types: provide the 128-bit integers used by current UAPI

The bundled linux/types.h shadows the toolchain's Linux header. New ARM64
ptrace headers use __u128, which the bundled copy did not define. Match the
kernel's integer definitions and alignment when the compiler supports int128.
Leave targets without int128, including 32-bit MIPS, unchanged.

--- a/include/linux/types.h
+++ b/include/linux/types.h
@@ -12,6 +12,11 @@
 #include <asm/types.h>
 #include <asm/posix_types.h>
 
+#ifdef __SIZEOF_INT128__
+typedef __signed__ __int128 __s128 __attribute__((aligned(16)));
+typedef unsigned __int128 __u128 __attribute__((aligned(16)));
+#endif
+
 #define __bitwise__
 #define __bitwise __bitwise__
 
